+# ATTACK.md — red team, loop `attack`, round 0 (run 20260921-224918)
+
+Target: `parseCsvLine` in `src/csv.mjs` (lines 19–88), judged against the
+contract in `README.md` lines 16–35. Node v25.2.1. All commands run bare from
+the project root with `node --input-type=module -e '...'`; nothing under
+`src/` or `tests/` was touched.
+
+Result: **no failing trace found.** `traces/` exists and is empty.
+
+## What was attacked
+
+### 1. Functional contract — differential against an independent reference
+
+I wrote a second parser directly from README.md lines 21–35 (a four-state
+machine: start-of-field / unquoted / quoted / after-closing-quote, with one
+trailing `\n` or `\r\n` stripped first) and compared it with `parseCsvLine`
+on:
+
+- **Exhaustive**: every string of length 0–8 over the alphabet
+  `{a , " \n \r}` — 488,281 inputs. 0 mismatches.
+- **Random exotic**: 300,000 strings of length 0–23 over
+  `{a b , " \n \r space TAB NUL U+FEFF lone-high-surrogate lone-low-surrogate
+  paired-surrogate U+2028 U+0085 \ ' ;}`. 0 mismatches.
+- **Structured**: 4,000 token-built strings of 1–5 KB mixing quoted fields,
+  `""` escapes, stray quotes, `\r`, `\n`, `\r\n`, NUL, surrogates, CJK.
+  0 mismatches.
+
+For every input the check also asserted the shape rule (README.md line
+16–19): success value is a plain `Array` whose every element is a `string`;
+failure is `instanceof CsvError`. Nothing else was ever thrown.
+
+Spot checks: the three README examples (lines 9–11) return exactly the
+documented arrays; `""` → `[""]`, `"\n"` → `[""]`, `"\r\n"` → `[""]`,
+`"\r"` → CsvError, `" a "` → `[" a "]`, `a"b` and ` "a"` → CsvError;
+`CsvError` is a direct subclass of `Error` with `name === "CsvError"`
+(src/csv.mjs lines 1–6).
+
+### 2. Non-string inputs (README.md line 19)
+
+`undefined`, missing argument, `null`, `0`, `1n`, `true`, `NaN`, a `Symbol`,
+`{}`, `[]`, `["a,b"]`, `new String("a,b")`, an object with a custom
+`toString`, an object with `Symbol.toPrimitive`, a function, a `Proxy`,
+`Object.create(null)`, a `Buffer`, a `Date`, a `RegExp`. All threw
+`TypeError` via the guard at src/csv.mjs line 20; none reached the parser.
+
+### 3. Performance (README.md line 18–19: never hangs, < 1 s at 100 KB)
+
+Twenty adversarial shapes, each generated at 100 KB, 1 MB and 10 MB to
+expose superlinear behaviour:
+
+all commas; plain unquoted; one quoted field made entirely of `""` escapes;
+the same unterminated; unterminated quote followed by plain text;
+unterminated quote followed by text dense with `""`; many `"a",` fields;
+many `"",` fields; quoted field alternating text and `""`; quoted field of
+commas; quoted field of `\r\n`; closing quote followed by junk at the very
+end; stray quote at the very end; `\r` at the very end; `\n\n` at the end;
+all commas then `\n`; surrogate pairs; lone surrogates with NUL; fields of
+`""""`; `a,a,a,...,"`.
+
+Worst case at 100 KB: 3.6 ms (all commas then `\n`). Worst at 10 MB:
+263 ms (unterminated quote followed by 3.3 M `""` pairs). Growth is linear
+across the three sizes for every shape, consistent with the single-pass
+`indexOf` loop at src/csv.mjs lines 43–56 and the per-unit scan at lines
+68–76. No hang, no stack growth (no recursion), no non-CsvError.
+
+## Not attacked / out of scope
+
+- Inputs near V8's maximum string length (~512 MB) or with hundreds of
+  millions of fields: the contract only bounds 100 KB, and an allocation
+  failure there would be a process OOM, not a thrown value. Not exercised.
+- Tampered globals (`String.prototype.indexOf`, `Array.prototype.push`).
+
+## Verdict
+
+pass — no input reproduced a violation of README.md lines 16–35.
