+# Changes
+
+## Round 0 (run 20260921-224918)
+
+No red-team traces exist yet: there is no `traces/` directory in round 0, so
+this round implements the README contract from scratch rather than fixing
+specific traces.
+
+### src/csv.mjs
+
+Replaced the toggle-based parser (which flipped a `quoted` flag on every `"`,
+accepted `a"b`, never threw `CsvError`, and used `rest.slice(1)` per character,
+making it quadratic) with a single-pass, index-based state machine that
+enforces every rule in README.md:
+
+- Fields split on `,`; empty text is `[""]`; trailing comma yields a trailing
+  empty field.
+- Quoted fields: `""` inside quotes is one `"`; commas, `\n`, `\r\n` and every
+  other character inside quotes are literal.
+- After a closing quote only `,`, the record terminator or end of text may
+  follow; anything else is a `CsvError`. An unclosed quote is a `CsvError`.
+- A `"` anywhere in an unquoted field is a `CsvError` (`a"b`, `a "b"`, ` "a"`).
+- Whitespace outside quotes is kept.
+- Exactly one trailing `\n` or `\r\n` is stripped before parsing; any other
+  unquoted `\r` or `\n` (including a lone trailing `\r`, or `\n\n`) is a
+  `CsvError`.
+- Everything else (tabs, NUL, control characters, U+2028/2029, BOM, lone
+  surrogates, non-ASCII quotes and separators) is literal.
+- Non-string input (including `String` objects and arrays) throws `TypeError`.
+
+The scan is linear in the input length, uses no recursion and no regexes, so
+it cannot hang or overflow the stack; a 100 KB record parses in well under a
+millisecond and a 6 MB record in ~60 ms.
+
+### tests/csv.test.mjs
+
+Kept the original four tests (folded into the new ones) and added one test per
+contract rule, plus:
+
+- an exhaustive check of every string up to length 6 over the alphabet
+  `a , " \n \r space` (~56k inputs) asserting the result is always an array of
+  strings or a `CsvError`, never anything else;
+- a quote/parse round trip over awkward field values;
+- timing tests over twelve 100 KB shapes (plain, quoted, all-commas, all
+  escaped quotes, late errors, unterminated quotes, Unicode) each required to
+  finish within a second, and a 6 MB record within five seconds.
+
+`npm test`: 19 tests, 19 pass.
